{{!
    @template local_pshub/session_lobby

    Where a learner waits for a class and walks into it.

    ONE ANSWER, ALWAYS WITH A REASON. Five refusals need five sentences and
    five different next steps: too early is a wait, full is a message to the
    teacher, lapsed access is a purchase, ended is a shrug, cancelled is news.
    A page that says only "you cannot join" has told nobody anything (§15).

    NO COUNTDOWN WITHOUT A CLOCK TO TRUST. The opening time is printed from the
    server's clock, and the server's current time is printed beside it, so a
    learner whose device is an hour out can see why the door is shut. A ticking
    countdown is an enhancement on top of that (PSH-S05-09), never the only
    way to know when the class starts - this page works with scripting off.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * coursename, courseurl, title, when, duration, servertime
    * canjoin, message, state - the verdict.
    * hasroom, joinurl, showroomnotice - whether there is anything to walk into.
    * hasopensat, opensat, opensin, opensistoday - when the door opens.
    * needsaccess, salesurl - the one refusal with something to buy.
    * islive - the class is happening now.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "coursename": "Anglais B1", "courseurl": "/local/pshub/learn/course.php?id=2",
        "title": "Séance 1", "when": "lundi 5 octobre, 18:00", "duration": "50 min",
        "servertime": "17:42",
        "canjoin": false, "message": "La salle ouvre 15 minutes avant le début.",
        "state": "tooearly",
        "hasroom": false, "showroomnotice": false,
        "hasopensat": true, "opensat": "17:45", "opensin": 180,
        "needsaccess": false, "salesurl": "/local/pshub/course.php?id=2",
        "islive": false
    }
}}
<div class="ps-page ps-page--narrow">

    <nav class="ps-crumb" aria-label="{{coursename}}">
        <a class="ps-crumb__link" href="{{courseurl}}">{{coursename}}</a>
        <span class="ps-crumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span class="ps-crumb__here">{{#str}}lobby_here, local_pshub{{/str}}</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="ps-lobby ps-lobby--{{state}}">

        {{#islive}}
            <span class="ps-lobby__live">{{#str}}learn_live_now, local_pshub{{/str}}</span>
        {{/islive}}

        <h1 class="ps-lobby__title">{{title}}</h1>
        <p class="ps-lobby__when">{{when}} · {{duration}}</p>

        {{#canjoin}}
            {{!
                The end-of-class warning, written by the clock at five minutes
                and again at two. A class that ends without warning is the
                complaint §8.3 exists to prevent; a warning that never arrives
                because scripting is off is a courtesy missed, not a breach.
            }}
            <p class="ps-lobby__warning" data-ps-endswarning="{{endswarning}}" hidden></p>

            {{#hasroom}}
                <a class="ps-btn ps-btn--navy ps-btn--big" href="{{joinurl}}">
                    {{#str}}join_ok, local_pshub{{/str}}
                </a>
                <p class="ps-lobby__note">{{#str}}lobby_joinnote, local_pshub{{/str}}</p>
            {{/hasroom}}
            {{#showroomnotice}}
                {{!
                    The door is open and there is nowhere to walk into: the
                    session has no BigBlueButton room yet. Better said than
                    offered as a button that opens nothing.
                }}
                <p class="ps-note ps-note--warn">{{#str}}lobby_noroom, local_pshub{{/str}}</p>
            {{/showroomnotice}}
        {{/canjoin}}

        {{^canjoin}}
            <p class="ps-lobby__message">{{message}}</p>

            {{#hasopensat}}
                <p class="ps-lobby__opens">
                    {{#opensistoday}}{{#str}}lobby_opensat, local_pshub, {{opensat}}{{/str}}{{/opensistoday}}
                    {{^opensistoday}}{{#str}}lobby_opensonday, local_pshub, {{opensat}}{{/str}}{{/opensistoday}}
                </p>
                {{!
                    Filled in by the clock when scripting is available, hidden
                    and empty otherwise - the sentence above already says when
                    the room opens.
                }}
                <p class="ps-lobby__countdown" data-ps-countdown hidden></p>
            {{/hasopensat}}

            {{#needsaccess}}
                <a class="ps-btn ps-btn--navy" href="{{salesurl}}">
                    {{#str}}lobby_seecourse, local_pshub{{/str}}
                </a>
            {{/needsaccess}}
            {{^needsaccess}}
                <a class="ps-btn ps-btn--outline" href="{{courseurl}}">
                    {{#str}}lobby_backtocourse, local_pshub{{/str}}
                </a>
            {{/needsaccess}}
        {{/canjoin}}

        {{!
            The server's own clock, printed small. It costs one line and it is
            the only way a learner whose device is an hour out can work out why
            the door is shut.
        }}
        <p class="ps-lobby__clock">{{#str}}lobby_servertime, local_pshub, {{servertime}}{{/str}}</p>

    </div>

</div>
